Z||000000||Raydar||11-20-2001||10:38 AM||||Seems like there was no federal law covering his actions. (Running in the exit.) <BR>All he can be charged with is disorderly conduct. A local misdemeanor. <BR>He had apparently already been through the security screening once, then ran to retrieve a camcorder that he had forgotten. <BR>When they caught up with him, he was quietly standing in line. Didn't even realize that all of the chaos going on was about <I>him.</I> <BR>I don't think he *even* imagined the repurcussions of his actions. <BR><P>------------------<BR>Raydar<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>From the Department of Redundancy Department.</FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000001||falconhulk||11-20-2001||11:33 AM||||I dont think it was that big a deal.  Sure they had to shut down for safety.  he did something he did NOT know or that any reasonalbe person would NOT know would result the way it did.  Give the guy a break.  Hes not an idiot he just did not want to lose an expensive camcorder.  Its the terrorists fault they have to shut things down now not his.  If he is fined or serves time an American is serving the sentence for the terrorist acts of Sept. 11.  Now that everyone knows of this story it wont happen again.  They should post signs and whatever else.  if it does happen again press charges on that person.||||reg||1
